\title{Feast of St. Michael and All Angels 2026}
\tag{cmc}
\date{2026-09-27}
\author{liamoc}
\quote{
Benedícite Dóminum, omnes Angeli eius, poténtes virtúte, qui fácitis verbum eius, ad audiéndam vocem sermónum eius. \br
In nómine Dómini omne genu flectátur, cæléstium, terréstrium et infernórum: quia Dominus factus obédiens usque ad mortem, mortem autem crucis: ídeo Dóminus Iesus Christus in glória est Dei Patris. \br
Omnia quæ fecísti nobis, Dómine, in vero iudício fecísti, quia peccávimus tibi, et mandátis tuis non obedívimus: sed da glóriam nómini tuo, et fac nobíscum secúndum multitúdinem misericórdiæ tuæ.
}

\p{This morning I was groggy after a night at the German club after my [Cloudburst](loc-005N) concert had wrapped up, but still cantored at [All Saints Ainslie](https://www.allsaintsainslie.org.au/) in a duet with our director Alasdair, singing Dering's [Duo Seraphin](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HRQK4jfyYJU): }
\quote{
\table{
  \tr{
    \td{Duo séraphim clamábant alter ad álterum:}
    \td{Two seraphs cry out one after another:}
  }
  \tr{
    \td{Sanctus, Sanctus, Sanctus Dóminus, Deus Sabaoth}
    \td{Holy, Holy, Holy Lord, God of Hosts}
  }
  \tr{
    \td{Plena est omnis terra glória eius.}
    \td{All the earth is full of his glory.}
  }
}
}
\p{We also came together in the evening with the rest of the choir to sing Evensong. I think we sang \em{exceptionally well} but only seven or so people came to hear it. We sang Stainer's [Hail, Gladdening Light](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hYmHdJJAyeA) as usual, as well as Phillip Moore's third service for the [Magnificat](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hRN08tkNN_k) and [Nunc Dimittis](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KTqucmeGPR4). For the preces and responses, we used Jack Oades' [lovely setting](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KPZ1-BdX9vM). The anthem was John Goss' [O Saviour of the World](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0QLS98Y47Vs): }
\quote{\poem{
  \line{O Saviour of the world,}
  \line{who by thy Cross and precious Blood}
  \line{hast redeemed us:}
  \line{Save us, and help us,}
  \line{we humbly beseech thee, O Lord.}
    \line{Amen.}
  }} 
\p{I'm still annoyed by the anticipation of the feast day, but I'll never get my way here.}